## candle — Apache-2.0 / MIT

Copyright (c) 2023 Hugging Face. https://github.com/huggingface/candle

The inference framework, and the Qwen3-TTS model itself: the talker, the code
predictor, the 12 Hz codec encoder and decoder, and the ECAPA-TDNN speaker
encoder live in `candle-transformers::models::qwen3_tts`. This backend supplies
the file layout, the protocol, and the streaming, and calls that model for
everything else. A later Qwen generation served here would come from that crate
the same way.

It is pinned to https://github.com/jorge-menjivar/candle at revision
8803b62d16965211e777e6ca9232d70cf81b11f6, which is upstream candle plus the
`qwen3_tts` module. `src/model.rs` follows the structure of that revision's
`candle-examples/examples/qwen3-tts/main.rs`, in particular the chunked decode
with left context that makes streamed audio identical to a single decode.


## Fetched at runtime, not redistributed here

These are downloaded by the Super TTS daemon on the user's machine before first
use, under their own terms; no part of them is contained in this repository or
its release archives.

  * The Qwen3-TTS checkpoints this version serves —
    `Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-0.6B-CustomVoice`,
    `Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-CustomVoice` and `Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-VoiceDesign`,
    each with the Qwen3-TTS-Tokenizer-12Hz codec — from
    https://huggingface.co/Qwen. Apache-2.0. Copyright Alibaba Cloud, Qwen team.
  * The `tokenizer.json` of https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B, Apache-2.0.
    The TTS repositories ship `vocab.json` and `merges.txt` but no assembled
    tokenizer, and the two vocabularies are the same one.
